{
  "_rule": "ARC-09-C81. The tier-2 names the roster writes and the bundled corpus does not contain, each excused by (file, identifier) with a reason from the closed set in tools/snowarch/lib/docs/identifiers.mjs REASONS; an example-field entry names its x_/u_ table, which the same file must write. A platform-prefixed name never appears here — it is the corpus name, the marker, a family glob, a glued name, or a rename. A name the corpus gains is stale and fails the check, so the list only shrinks unless an example invents something. ARC-09-C104: two more shapes take an entry. A `script-code` entry names a dotted pair in a sentence about example code (`current.approval`), and only a variable can — its left half has no underscore, because a table written with a word is a claim about the table and is reworded in the corpus's own words or marked. A CamelCase name on a line that claims baseline takes example-name or payload-key when the example invented it (`AceGrid`). The field is `identifier`, not `token`: tests/never-commit.test.mjs reads a JSON key named token as a credential. ARC-09-C144: a name written as words — a flow, an action, a script or an alias an example invents (\"Daily Feedback Request Sweep\") — takes example-name, keyed by its spelling as written; a platform name written as words is the corpus's name or carries the marker, never an entry.",
  "_glued": "Names the corpus prints glued to their label (\"SIU Tasksn\\_ins\\_siu\\_task\"), so a whole-name lookup cannot see them. Each entry carries the glued spelling and the page; the check confirms the page still prints it, and the entry is stale the day upstream fixes the page. Measured 2026-10-04 (the architect): 102 corpus names have the shape <label>sn_…, and for 33 the glued form is the only occurrence; one is written by the roster. There is no general un-gluing rule: it would also read `system_owner` as `em_owner`.",
  "glued": [
    {"identifier":"sn_ins_siu_task","glued":"tasksn_ins_siu_task","page":"markdown/financial-services-operations/insurance-claims/components-installed-personal-lines-claims.md"}
  ],
